  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Implemented a lazy synchronous SharedArrayBuffer renderer client and a persistent offline Playwright worker. One browser/page is reused, Chromium closes after 60 seconds idle and recycles after 100 jobs, one retry is allowed for a reported browser/page crash, and shutdown disposes through the save-hook lifecycle and process beforeExit. Fixed request/output bounds and timeout behavior, including a header-only error protocol that remains safe with a one-byte response buffer. Focused fake-worker tests cover reuse, busy rejection, timeout/hard-exit fallback, one crash restart, stable second-crash failure, limits, tiny buffers, and disposal. Real Chromium validation produced byte-identical cold/warm PNGs, a valid SVG, a prompt beforeExit shutdown, and a 3.10x three-image warm speedup (8719.4 ms cold versus 2812.3 ms warm).",
    "risks": [
      "A native hard worker exit cannot be observed by a main-thread exit callback while Atomics.wait blocks; it deliberately resolves as the bounded timeout and is terminated without retry, while reported browser/page crashes retry exactly once.",
      "The required full integration tier ran and the graphics capability/export tests passed, but the tier failed in unrelated native-kernel and performance tests because this branch lacks a matching production native-kernel cache; the fresh failing receipt is retained."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Register test/graphics-export-worker.cjs in the central test manifest from the integration lane; this task intentionally has no manifest claim.",
      "Rerun pnpm test:integration after publishing a production native-kernel cache matching this branch, then set the task contract to review."
    ]
  }
